 [case id=store-code-001-put-get-def level=core
  [tags store mem code-identity computation-id put-blob opaque f1-prime]
  [; F1' (ruled 2026-08-08): code is an OPAQUE document — stored byte-exact
     by put-blob (identity = hash of the RAW bytes). COMPUTATION identity
     ("same function?") is orthogonal and survives storage trivially,
     because the bytes do: the claim recomputed on the retrieved source
     equals the claim on the original. The def here is the representative
     that MANGLES through the structured path (string-literal body), so
     this pins the opaque carriage, not a lucky canonicalization survivor.
     Byte-exactness itself is pinned by store-blob-001; this replaces the
     retired put-def/get-def round-trip. ]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?let [= $s [$store:open "mem://"]] [= $src "[?def greet ($name) [str-format 'hello, {}' $name]]"] [$eq [$cx:computation-id [$store:get-blob $s [$store:put-blob $s $src]]] [$cx:computation-id $src]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
true
#]]
 ]

