 [; ── (D) text doc-I/O enabling verbs (#78 CSRP) — put-doc-text / get-doc-text.
    A CX-program CSRP server has no ast_bin/parse-text→doc verb, so it handles
    cxd-text bodies via these. put-doc-text canonicalizes its text (parse +
    render-canonical) then hashes+stores, so it dedups with put-doc of the same
    doc (one stored object). get-doc-text returns the stored canonical text, or
    the absence channel () for a miss (never null, never an err). mem:// is
    capability-free, so these run under the empty set. ── ]

