 [; store-029 (csrp-handle cap-denied) RETIRED with the CSRP data plane
    (stream-4 S3): the verb is gone — the store service wire is the XSP
    store profile (cx-store://) with the gRPC edge. ]

 [; ── the computation-identity cache (stream 5, #677 — L102/L106,
    computation_identity.md). The [computation] record is constructed
    IN-LANGUAGE from shipped pieces (cx:computation-id, cx:hash, store
    addresses, cx:env, caps); the cache is an alias in the
    computation/<addr> namespace on the EXISTING alias verbs — no new
    store API. Admission into that namespace validates FAIL-LOUD:
    the name must be the record Tier-1 address of a stored, well-shaped
    record (CXER1117); the record fn must resolve to a stored def that
    declares pure AND passes the checker, with the Tier-2 claim
    recomputing (CXER1118); the aliased result must not be a
    never-cacheable err class — the CXER0270-0279 runtime-environment
    band + host-tunable CXER0153 (CXER1119). Assertions are
    version-agnostic (no literal addresses: cx:env varies by build). ]

 [case id=store-comp-001-m5-end-to-end level=core
  [tags store computation cache m5 L102 L106 stream-5]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?def price-order scope=public pure [returns float] ($o) [* $o/qty $o/price]]
[?let
 [= $src '[?def price-order scope=public pure [returns float] ($o) [* $o/qty $o/price]]']
 [= $s [$store:open 'mem://m5']]
 [= $fsrc [$store:put-blob $s $src]]
 [= $order [$store:put-doc-text $s '[order [qty 3] [price 4.5]]']]
 [= $rec {computation: {fn: {code: [$cx:computation-id $src], source: $fsrc}, inputs: {order: $order}, env: [$cx:env], caps: [$caps]}}]
 [= $rid [$store:put-doc $s $rec]]
 [= $price [$price-order [order [qty 3] [price 4.5]]]]
 [= $result [$store:put-doc $s [total $price]]]
 [= $set [$store:set-alias $s [$concat 'computation/' $rid] $result]]
 [= $hit [$store:get-alias $s [$concat 'computation/' $rid]]]
 [= $rec2 {computation: {fn: {code: [$cx:computation-id $src], source: $fsrc}, inputs: {order: [$store:put-doc-text $s '[order [qty   3] [price   4.5]]']}, env: [$cx:env], caps: [$caps]}}]
 [r [$eq [$cx:hash $rec] $rid]
    [$eq $hit $result]
    [$eq [$store:get-doc $s $hit] [total 13.5]]
    [$eq [$cx:hash $rec2] $rid]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[r true true true true]
#]]
 ]
note: the four assertions — the record doc address IS its plain Tier-1
note: (put-doc of canonical text = cx:hash, no computation: prefix, no
note: new registry row); the explicit store-mediated lookup returns the
note: bound result; the cached value reads back; and a REFORMATTED order
note: (same canonical text) yields the SAME computation address — the
note: M5 reformat-is-a-hit property, with zero literal addresses so the
note: case is build-version-agnostic.

 [case id=store-comp-002-impure-fn-refused level=core
  [tags store computation cache negative impure CXER1118 L106 stream-5]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?let
 [= $src '[?def f scope=public impure [returns any] ($x) $x]']
 [= $s [$store:open 'mem://imp']]
 [= $fsrc [$store:put-blob $s $src]]
 [= $in [$store:put-doc $s [v 1]]]
 [= $rec {computation: {fn: {code: [$cx:computation-id $src], source: $fsrc}, inputs: {x: $in}, env: [$cx:env], caps: [$caps]}}]
 [= $rid [$store:put-doc $s $rec]]
 [= $result [$store:put-doc $s [v 1]]]
 [$store:set-alias $s [$concat 'computation/' $rid] $result]]
#]]
  [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER1118
#]]
 ]

