 [case id=store-comp-004-uncacheable-result-refused level=core
  [tags store computation cache negative never-cached CXER1119 L106 stream-5]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?def g scope=public pure [returns any] ($x) $x]
[?let
 [= $src '[?def g scope=public pure [returns any] ($x) $x]']
 [= $s [$store:open 'mem://nc']]
 [= $fsrc [$store:put-blob $s $src]]
 [= $in [$store:put-doc $s [v 1]]]
 [= $rec {computation: {fn: {code: [$cx:computation-id $src], source: $fsrc}, inputs: {x: $in}, env: [$cx:env], caps: [$caps]}}]
 [= $rid [$store:put-doc $s $rec]]
 [; CO-2 migration: storing a bare err document is a deliberate act — the
    setup step names it with errs=:permit so the case still reaches the
    CXER1119 uncacheable-result refusal it exists to pin. ]
 [= $bad [$store:put-doc-text $s "[err code='cx-err:CXER0273' message='evaluation budget exceeded']" {errs: :permit}]]
 [$store:set-alias $s [$concat 'computation/' $rid] $bad]]
#]]
  [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER1119
#]]
 ]
note: budget exhaustion is input-INDEPENDENT state (the never-cached
note: class): caching it would serve a host artifact as the computation
note: answer. Input-dependent [err]s (divide-by-zero) remain cacheable —
note: they are deterministic per the pure => deterministic theorem.

 [case id=store-comp-005-env-axis-discriminates level=core
  [tags store computation identity env-axis L103 stream-5]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?let
 [= $e [$cx:env]]
 [= $mk [?fn $rt {computation: {fn: {code: 'computes-as:sha2-256:ab', source: 'sha2-256:cd'}, inputs: {x: 'sha2-256:ef'}, env: {builtins: $e/builtins, runtime: $rt, schema-dialect: '0.8'}, caps: {}}}]]
 [r [$eq [$cx:hash [$mk '1.0.0']] [$cx:hash [$mk '1.0.0']]]
    [$eq [$cx:hash [$mk '1.0.0']] [$cx:hash [$mk '1.0.1']]]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[r true false]
#]]
 ]
note: the patch-bump axis pinned without a rebuild: identical records
note: hash identically; a runtime PATCH difference alone moves the
note: address (a patch can fix a determinism bug — cold cache, never a
note: wrong answer).

 [case id=store-comp-006-field-order-irrelevant level=core
  [tags store computation identity canonicalization map L102 stream-5]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[$eq
 [$cx:hash {computation: {fn: {code: 'computes-as:sha2-256:ab', source: 'sha2-256:cd'}, inputs: {x: 'sha2-256:ef'}, env: {runtime: '1.0.0'}, caps: {}}}]
 [$cx:hash {computation: {caps: {}, env: {runtime: '1.0.0'}, inputs: {x: 'sha2-256:ef'}, fn: {source: 'sha2-256:cd', code: 'computes-as:sha2-256:ab'}}}]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
true
#]]
 ]
note: the L102 map-shaped-record rationale pinned: field containers are
note: maps, self-canonicalizing under the canonical key sort — no
note: bespoke field order to specify or drift.

 [case id=store-comp-007-meta-does-not-move-id level=core
  [tags store computation identity meta L102 stream-5 708]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?let
 [= $s [$store:open 'mem://meta']]
 [= $plain [$store:put-doc $s [order [qty 3]]]]
 [= $meta  [$store:put-doc $s [?meta {reviewed: true} [order [qty 3]]]]]
 [$eq $plain $meta]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
true
#]]
 ]
note: meta-does-not-participate at the STORE boundary (the #708 item-1
note: lane-1 exclusion riding into the record: a VALUE annotated [?meta]
note: keeps its store address, so the computation address holds — the M5
note: meta => hit negative, pinned via input-address equality. The lane-1
note: form is the EVALUATED annotation (idh-032); a raw-text document
note: carrying a literal [?meta …] node is data, not an annotation.


 [# ── store-cst-001..004: the stream-7 consistency floor on store open
       (consistency_vocabulary.md L122/L123/F5, #679/#714): declare-and-verify
       at open-opts, the F5 linearizable-ref write discipline, and the shared
       teaching-refusal authority. ──────────────────────────────────────── #]

 [case id=store-cst-001-floor-declared-satisfied level=core gate=enforced
  [tags store consistency floor declare-and-verify stream-7 679 L123]
  [; the store floor: tokens the surface advertises are accepted at open,
     echoed on the handle, and the handle behaves normally. ]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?let [= $s [$store:open-opts "mem://" {consistency: (:linearizable-ref, :read-your-writes, :monotonic-reads)}]]
[= $h [$store:put-doc $s [doc [item "x"]]]]
  [floor tokens=$s@consistency ok=[$store:exists $s $h]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[floor tokens=':linearizable-ref :read-your-writes :monotonic-reads' ok=true]
#]]
 ]

 [case id=store-cst-002-linearizable-ref-write-discipline level=core gate=enforced
  [tags store consistency linearizable-ref F5 CXER4990 discriminator-pair stream-7 679 714]
  [; the F5 pair on one root: an UNDECLARED handle keeps the silent LWW
     set-alias (pre-vocabulary behavior); a declaring handle refuses
     expect-less set-alias AND branch-force at stage write, while plain
     branch (fast-forward guarded — the CAS discipline) stays available. ]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?let [= $u [$store:open "mem://"]]
[= $h1 [$store:put-doc $u [doc [v 1]]]]
[= $h2 [$store:put-doc $u [doc [v 2]]]]
[= $a1 [$store:set-alias $u "head" $h1]]
[= $a2 [$store:set-alias $u "head" $h2]]
[= $d [$store:open-opts "mem://" {consistency: (:linearizable-ref)}]]
[= $g1 [$store:put-doc $d [doc [v 1]]]]
[= $b [$store:branch $d "main" $g1]]
[= $r1 [?fallback [$store:set-alias $d "main" $g1]
  [recover-with [refused op=set-alias code=$err/@code stage=$err/context/stage token=$err/context/token]]]]
[= $r2 [?fallback [$store:branch-force $d "main" $g1]
  [recover-with [refused op=branch-force code=$err/@code]]]]
  [pair lww=[$store:get-alias $u "head"] branch-name=$b@name $r1 $r2]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[pair lww='sha2-256:34bb7bd03048150a5f9b3fc52fb264f378d71d6f03a1ac0b0bfbdab43d1dac35' branch-name=main [refused op=set-alias code=cx-err:CXER4990 stage=:write token=:linearizable-ref] [refused op=branch-force code=cx-err:CXER4990]]
#]]
 ]

 [case id=store-cst-003-linearizable-ref-delete-refused level=core gate=enforced
  [tags store consistency linearizable-ref delete-alias F5 CXER4990 stream-7 679 714]
  [; ref deletion has no expect-bearing form, so a declaring handle refuses
     it — CAS-only means CAS-only. ]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?let [= $d [$store:open-opts "mem://" {consistency: (:linearizable-ref)}]]
[= $h [$store:put-doc $d [doc [v 1]]]]
[= $b [$store:branch $d "main" $h]]
[?fallback [$store:delete-alias $d "main"]
  [recover-with [refused code=$err/@code stage=$err/context/stage token=$err/context/token]]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[refused code=cx-err:CXER4990 stage=:write token=:linearizable-ref]
#]]
 ]

 [case id=store-cst-004-teaching-refusal-shared-authority level=core gate=enforced
  [tags store consistency exactly-once teaching-refusal CXER4990 stream-7 679 L122]
  [; ONE vocabulary authority across surfaces: the store floor answers the
     SAME exactly-once teaching refusal as the journal floor, naming
     [idempotent]. ]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?fallback [$store:open-opts "mem://" {consistency: (:exactly-once)}]
  [recover-with [refused code=$err/@code token=$err/context/token answer=$err/context/answer]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[refused code=cx-err:CXER4990 token=:exactly-once answer='[idempotent]']
#]]
 ]

 [case id=store-mig-001-batch-migration-mechanics level=core gate=enforced
  [tags store migration modify-doc using dedup claim stream-21 693 L148 L152]
  [; stored-doc migration = get, pure transform, put, ref advance — and
     stores migrate in BATCH, non-destructively by construction: the
     transform is modify-doc with a pure using-FN; the new doc gets its
     own content address; the OLD doc remains addressable (immutable
     substrate — nothing is overwritten, migration is always additive);
     re-migrating the unchanged doc yields the SAME address (dedup makes
     it free); and the migration provenance is a Lane-2 claim VALUE
     linking new to old BY CONTENT ADDRESS — a plain stored value, never
     store metadata, the same hash-linkage discipline the journal's
     supersedes vocabulary uses. ]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?let [= $s [$store:open "mem://se-mig1"]]
[= $h1 [$store:put-doc $s [order id="A-1" total=107]]]
[= $h2 [$store:modify-doc $s $h1 [using [?fn ($d) [order id=$d@id subtotal=[- $d@total 10] tax=10]]]]]
[= $od [$store:get-doc $s $h1]]
[= $old-alive [= $od@total 107]]
[= $h3 [$store:modify-doc $s $h1 [using [?fn ($d) [order id=$d@id subtotal=[- $d@total 10] tax=10]]]]]
[= $claim [migrated-from hash=$h1 to=$h2]]
[= $ch [$store:put-doc $s $claim]]
[= $back [$store:get-doc $s $ch]]
  [probe distinct=[!= $h1 $h2] old-alive=$old-alive dedup=[= $h2 $h3] claim-links=[= $back@hash $h1]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[probe distinct=true old-alive=true dedup=true claim-links=true]
#]]
 ]

 [; ── stream 20 (#692, erasure_compliance §3/§4): the reserved subject
    vocabulary on the write surface. A payload carrying subject= MUST carry a
    ≥128-bit CSPRNG nonce= (the digest-oracle defense) — missing/short/derived
    = CXER4619, never a warning (audit C7: dedup/parity witnesses alone pass
    for nonce=1). Custody is fail-closed: a plaintext store refuses a subject
    declaration it could never crypto-shred (CXER1144). The sealed round-trip
    + shred + rotation-balance behavior is pinned at the V layer
    (store_subject_test.v) — it needs env KEK custody.]

 [case id=store-subject-001-nonce-required level=core gate=enforced
